---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Talent Acquisition
description: A higher-touch search practice for roles where volume hiring won't work — specialized, senior, or hard-to-fill positions.
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/count-up.js
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   TALENT ACQUISITION — Hallmark audit pass, matching job-placement.njk.

   Hero drops the aurora/dot background; section heads are single-column with the
   label directly above the heading; the "what's included" grid is a definition
   list with inline icons on hairline rules. The premium framing (PRD §6) is now
   carried by the bg-surface tone on the hero + opening section and the generous
   section rhythm alone — not by the decorative hero field.
   ================================================================ #}

{% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { label: "Talent Acquisition" }] %}

{# ---------- Hero — on bg-surface, the one-shade lift off paper. ---------- #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-surface">
  <div class="section-container pb-14 pt-8 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-12">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <p class="eyebrow">Confidential, retained search</p>

        <h1 class="mt-4 font-grotesk text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl">
          Precision hiring for roles that matter.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead-copy mt-5 max-w-xl">
          A confidential, retained search practice for leadership and specialized
          roles — built to reach the candidate who was never going to apply, not
          just the one who did.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="{{ '/contact/?role=employer' | url }}" class="btn-primary">
            {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }} Start a search
          </a>
          <a href="{{ '/services/recruitment-staffing/' | url }}" class="btn-outline">
            Compare with staffing
          </a>
        </div>

        {# TODO: confirm these figures with the client before launch — see stats.json. #}
        <dl class="mt-10 grid max-w-lg grid-cols-3 gap-4 border-t border-ink/10 pt-6">
          {% for stat in stats.list.slice(0, 3) %}
          <div>
            <dd class="stat-figure text-xl sm:text-2xl"
                data-count-up data-target="{{ stat.value }}" data-suffix="{{ stat.suffix }}">0{{ stat.suffix }}</dd>
            <dt class="stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</dt>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="relative lg:col-span-5">
        {% set coverImage = images.services["talent-acquisition"].cover %}
        <div class="glass-panel p-3">
          <img src="{{ coverImage.url }}"
               alt="{{ coverImage.alt }}"
               width="1400" height="933" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
               class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-[1.1rem] object-cover">
        </div>

        {# Frost, not pane — it floats over the photograph. See THEME.md §3. #}
        <div class="glass-frost absolute -bottom-4 left-6 rounded-2xl px-5 py-3.5 sm:-left-6">
          <p class="meta">Engagement</p>
          <p class="font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Retained</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- How this differs from staffing ----------
   The most important block on the page: if a visitor can't tell the two services
   apart in five seconds, both pages fail. On the same bg-surface tone as the hero
   so the two read as one uninterrupted opening statement. ---------- #}
<section id="difference" class="scroll-mt-28 bg-surface py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="assertion sm:text-3xl">
        Staffing fills a role you have. Search finds the person who was never going to apply.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="ledger min-w-[40rem]">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Recruitment &amp; Staffing</th>
            <th scope="col">Talent Acquisition</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% set comparison = [
            { k: "What it does", a: "Fills a defined role from an existing pool", b: "Builds a pipeline for a role that doesn't have one" },
            { k: "Timeline", a: "Days to weeks", b: "6–10 weeks" },
            { k: "Candidates", a: "Actively looking", b: "Usually not looking" },
            { k: "Best for", a: "Volume, contract, defined roles", b: "Leadership, specialized, competitive roles" },
            { k: "Terms", a: "Contingency", b: "Retained" }
          ] %}
          {% for row in comparison %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-rowhead>{{ row.k }}</th>
            <td class="pr-6">{{ row.a }}</td>
            <td class="font-medium text-ink">{{ row.b }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 meta leading-relaxed">
      Filling a defined role quickly? <a href="{{ '/services/recruitment-staffing/' | url }}" class="text-brand hover:underline">Recruitment &amp; Staffing</a> is the faster route.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- What's included ---------- #}
<section id="included" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="section-title">What a retained search includes.</h2>
    <p class="lead-copy mt-4">A higher-touch practice for roles where a job posting was never going to be enough.</p>
  </div>

  {% set included = [
    { icon: "target", t: "Executive & specialized search", d: "Dedicated, retained search for leadership and niche technical roles — not a contingency posting run in parallel by three other firms." },
    { icon: "users", t: "Passive candidate sourcing", d: "Direct, confidential outreach to people who aren't job-searching — where the strongest candidates for a senior role usually are." },
    { icon: "chart", t: "Market mapping", d: "A clear view of where the right candidates sit today, and what it takes to reach them." },
    { icon: "support", t: "Long-term partnership model", d: "A dedicated search partner who knows the role and the team, not a transactional vendor relationship." }
  ] %}
  <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-7 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {% for item in included %}
    <div class="flex gap-4 border-t border-ink/15 pt-5">
      <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand">{{ icon(item.icon, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
      <div>
        <dt class="card-title">{{ item.t }}</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 body-copy">{{ item.d }}</dd>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
</section>

{# ---------- Market mapping ----------
   The deliverable that justifies the premium framing, so it gets a real zig-zag —
   a photograph and room to describe it in full sentences. ---------- #}
<section id="map" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="section-title">What a market map gives you.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-5 sm:items-center">
      <div class="sm:col-span-3">
        <p class="body-copy text-[17px]">
          Who's doing this job today and where, what they're paid, which
          companies are the realistic feeder pool, and how long a move from
          each typically takes.
        </p>
        <p class="highlight mt-7">You keep it whether or not you hire through us.</p>
      </div>

      {% set plate = images.services["talent-acquisition"].plate %}
      <figure class="glass-panel overflow-hidden sm:col-span-2">
        <img src="{{ plate.url }}" alt="{{ plate.alt }}"
             width="{{ plate.width }}" height="{{ plate.height }}" loading="lazy"
             class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover">
        <figcaption class="meta px-4 pb-4 pt-3">{{ plate.caption }}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- The process ---------- #}
<section id="procedure" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Step by step</p>
    <h2 class="section-title mt-2">A search built around the role.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
    {% set steps = [
      { label: "Discovery", description: "Understand the role, the team, and what success looks like a year in." },
      { label: "Market mapping", description: "Identify where qualified candidates actually are." },
      { label: "Outreach", description: "Direct, confidential approach to passive candidates." },
      { label: "Shortlist", description: "A small, vetted slate — not a wide net." },
      { label: "Placement", description: "Offer support and a 6-month replacement guarantee." }
    ] %}
    {% include "partials/process-timeline.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

{% set faqKey = "talent-acquisition" %}
{% set faqTitle = "Before you commission a search." %}
{% include "partials/faq-accordion.njk" %}

{% set ctaStamp = "Ready when you are" %}
{% set ctaHeadline = "Have a role that's hard to fill?" %}
{% set ctaSubtext = "Let's talk about what a dedicated search would look like." %}
{% set ctaLabel = "Start a Conversation" %}
{% set ctaHref = "/contact/?role=employer" %}
{% include "partials/cta-section.njk" %}
